German car manufacturer [[Audi]] has competed in [[Formula One]] as a [[List of Formula One constructors|constructor]] and [[List of Formula One engine manufacturers|power unit manufacturer]] since {{F1|2026}}. Their current iteration, '''Audi Motorsport AG''', competing as '''Audi Revolut F1 Team''', was formed through the acquisition of [[Sauber Motorsport]], with [[Audi V6 hybrid Formula One power unit|power units developed by]] '''Audi Formula Racing GmbH'''.

Prior to [[World War II]], Audi's predecessor [[Auto Union]] contested [[Grand Prix motor racing]] from [[1935 Grand Prix season|1935]] to [[1939 Grand Prix season|1939]]. Audi announced their intention to acquire Sauber—who debuted in {{F1|1993}}—and its Swiss facilities in 2022, ahead of [[2026 Formula One World Championship#Regulation changes|new power unit and chassis regulations in 2026]]. The project expanded to a [[Formula One engines|power unit]] facility in [[Bavaria]] and a technology centre in the "[[Glossary of motorsport terms#M|Motorsport Valley]]" of [[Oxfordshire]], England.

== Background ==
=== Pre–World War II Grands Prix (1935–1939) ===
